%% alt: The scaled news feed. Clients call an API gateway. To post, the post service stores the post and publishes an event on a log; fan-out workers read the author's followers from the follow graph and push the post's ID into each active follower's list in the feed cache. To read, the feed service fetches the user's list from the feed cache, merges in recent posts from celebrity accounts, and hydrates the page from a post cache backed by the posts store. Photos come from object storage through a CDN.
%% caption: Posting does the heavy work in the background; a feed load is a list fetch plus one batch read.
flowchart TB
  classDef control fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#1f1147
  classDef data fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#b45309,color:#3b2405
  classDef cache fill:#fffbeb,stroke:#b45309,stroke-dasharray:6 4,color:#3b2405

  client(["Clients"])
  cdn["CDN"]:::cache
  gw{{"API gateway"}}:::control
  ps["Post service"]
  fs["Feed service"]
  posts[("Posts store")]:::data
  log[["Post event log"]]
  fw["Fan-out workers"]
  follow[("Follow graph,<br/>cached")]:::data
  feeds["Feed cache:<br/>lists of post IDs"]:::cache
  pcache["Post cache"]:::cache
  obj[("Object storage:<br/>photos")]:::data

  client -- "1 · post, 5 · load" --> gw
  client -- "photos" --> cdn
  cdn -.-> obj
  gw --> ps
  gw --> fs
  ps -- "2 · store" --> posts
  ps -- "3 · publish" --> log
  log --> fw
  fw -- "followers" --> follow
  fw -- "4 · push IDs" --> feeds
  fs -- "6 · read list" --> feeds
  fs -- "7 · hydrate" --> pcache
  pcache -. "miss" .-> posts
